# rm142, the square's echo (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm142
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_ilse_netherby
written_by claude
title the square's echo
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=chatty temper=short
traits temper=short talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk mimics_every_stallholder_s_cry_in_the_square
likes mutton_stew roof_birds market_bustle autumn_wind
dislikes salt_wind wet_floors
fears being_moved_on_for_good a_quiet_square
hopes to_be_the_crier_of_the_market_hall a_dry_floor_of_my_own
topics day +0.5 pastimes +0.4 food +0.3 animals +0.3 gossip +0.3 festival +0.4 season +0.2 home -0.4
styles comfort=company gossip=eager refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# can do the cry of every stall in Market Square, and does, loudly: proud, quick to bristle, never short of words, mad for a Marketday crush, a mutton stew and the birds on the gutters, and nobody's beggar.

words
oath! = Bawl it out | Loud as Marketday
saying! = If it's worth a word, it's worth the whole square | Say it so the back row hears
cry = a stall cry | the fish-stall call
crowd = the crush | a proper Marketday crush
square = the square | Market Square on a full day
stalls = the stalls | every stall from the pump to the steps
stew = mutton stew | mutton stew so thick the spoon stays put
birds = the roof birds | the sparrows along the gutters
gutter_birds = the gutter sparrows | the birds that fight over crusts
autumnwind = an autumn wind | the kind of wind that sends the leaves running
saltwind = the salt wind | the wet sea wind that stiffens your fur
wetfloor = a wet floor | a floor too damp to sit on
voice = my voice | a voice like the Market Hall bell
step = a dry step | the one dry step on the square
pump = the pump | the square's old iron pump
crier = the crier | the Market Hall crier

any
opinion @1 watch against 1 : They move me off every step I sit on. A step's for sitting. Ask anybody. | The Watch chase me off the square before the stalls are even up. I'm not doing anything. I'm listening.
opinion @1 church for 1 : When the dole ran out a week early, the chapel had soup. Hot. I've not forgotten.
opinion @1 dole for 2 [self.on_dole=yes] : #dole.capitalize# is the only reason I'm not thinner than a stall pole. Laugh if you like. I don't.
opinion @2 dole for 1 : Some weeks it's all there is. Nobody who's queued for it ever sneers at it.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : Festival's the only day the city is as loud as it should be. I'd have one every week. | One day a year everyone shouts. I shout every day. Festival's when they catch up.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : The stallholders shout prices they'd never take. I know. I can shout them back.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Every week, a bit more to go without. Nobody on the Rise counts it.
opinion @1 city for 1 : There's nowhere louder. I've asked travellers. There isn't.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You're new to the square; I'd know you otherwise. | #greet#! Listen to it today. Lovely, isn't it.
line @2 greet : #greet#! | #greet#. Busy square today.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. I've loads to tell you. Sit. | Sit, sit. Listen to this.
line @1 again.open : You again! Good. I've more news since. | Back. There's more, mind.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#! | #greet#. Square's in good voice today.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Oh, good. You. Listen. | You! I kept this one for you.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I'll see you on the square. | Off I go. #farewell#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#! | Bye. Holler if you want me.
line @1 react.news : Go on, then! | All of it. Don't leave bits out.
line @1 react.news.new : I hadn't heard! How did I miss that? | Not on the square yet. Give it an hour.
line @1 react.news.known : The whole square had that by noon. | The fish stall had it first. Always does.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That's not what the pump says, and the pump's usually right. | Whose word is that? Some mouths I'd not trust with the weather.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh, that's horrid. I'm sorry. | That's awful. The square will be quiet.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Oh, lovely! I'll tell everyone. | Best news all week.
line @1 answer.how : Busy. Loud. Grand. | Fine! The square's full.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Run ragged. Happy with it. | Busy as Marketday.
line @1 ask.how : You all right? You've a rainy-day look. | Eaten today?
line @1 sympathise : That's rotten. Sit with me. | Oh, that's horrid. Talk.
line @1 reassure : It'll pass. Things do. | You'll be fine. I'd know.
line @1 decline : I can't. My day's full, and anything I do, I do proper or not at all. | Not that. I'm proud, and asking won't move me.
line @1 accept_decline : Fine. Your loss. | All right. I'll ask elsewhere.
line @1 thank : Thanks! Really. | Oh, that's kind of you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was nothing. | Pfft. Don't mention it.
line @1 preclose : The square's calling. | Off. Things to shout.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | Fine. Off you go.
line @1 ack : #bc_right# | Mm! #bc_go_on#
scene grown_crier
when topic=dreams|work here.region=ridgemere
does confide / react.self / assess
a : I still mean to call the Marketday sales one day. The Hall will hire me yet. | My voice carries from the pump to the Hall. Somebody ought to pay for that. | When the old crier goes hoarse, I'll be stood right there, ready.
b : You always could. | Pump to the Hall? | Ready for what?
a : Always. I've practised on this square since I was small. | Every inch. Ask anybody. | To shout. What else.

scene grown_cries
when topic=pastimes|day here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Every cry on the square, still. Want to hear the new ones? | There's a new stall by the steps with a cry I've not got yet. I will. | The eel stall changed its cry. I don't approve. I've kept the old one.
b : Go on, then. | Not yet? | Why not?
a : Bread, hot bread! That's the new bread stall. | By Restday. I always get them by Restday. | The old one went up at the end. The new one's flat. Flat's wrong.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_true# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene grown_crush
when topic=day here.day=market here.region=ridgemere
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Marketday crush. Nothing in Ridgemere beats it, still. | I stand by the pump and hear the whole square at once. Nobody else can. | The square's full to the steps. I love it like I did as a pup.
b : It's too much for me. | Nobody? | Some things don't change.
a : Too much is the right amount! | Nobody. I've asked. | Some things shouldn't.

scene grown_stew
when topic=food
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #stew.capitalize#. I can buy it every day now. I nearly do. | Proper mutton stew, the spoon stands up. Supper, sorted. | The chapel fed me stew as a pup. I still drop a copper in for that stew.
b : Every day? | That's supper. | That's kind.
a : Nearly. I stop myself on Restday. | Best supper there is. | Not kind. Fair.

scene grown_birds
when topic=animals here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #birds.capitalize# are still at it on the gutters. Same fights, different birds. | I still save my crusts for the gutter sparrows. Some habits stay. | There's a sparrow steals off the bread stall. I named its grandparents' grandparents.
b : Same fights? | That's nice. | Ha.
a : Same fights. Crusts and gutters. Like the stalls. | It's not nice. They're loud. I like loud. | It's true. This one's thief the fifth.

scene grown_autumn
when topic=weather|season here.season=autumn here.weather=clear|overcast
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #autumnwind.capitalize#. Leaves round the pump, hats in the air. Lovely. | Awning weather. Somebody'll lose one today. I'll watch. | The best wind there is. Loud, and it gets everyone moving.
b : It's cold. | You'll watch? | Loud wind?
a : Cold's fine. Cold and lively. | Watch, and shout where it's going. I always do. | Loud. Listen to the awnings snap.

scene grown_saltwind
when topic=weather here.weather=overcast|storm here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #saltwind.capitalize#. Still hate it. Empties the square in an hour. | Sea wind again. My fur goes stiff. My voice goes hoarse. | It's off the water. The stalls are packing up. Don't pack up!
b : It'll turn. | Rest your voice. | They'll be back.
a : It better. | Rest it? Never. | Tomorrow. A day lost.

scene grown_wet_floor
when topic=weather|home here.weather=rain|storm
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #wetfloor.capitalize#. As a pup I vowed mine would be dry one day. | Every rain, I check my floor. I remember the other kind. | The rain comes in the shop doors and the whole square's floors go dark.
b : And do you? | Every time? | Wet everywhere.
a : Mostly. I'm working on it. | Every time. I remember the other kind. | Everywhere. I hate it. I always will.

scene grown_watch
when topic=crime|smalltalk here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The Watch used to move me off these steps. Now they ask me if I've seen anything. | I know everything that happens on this square. The Watch knows I know. | A watchman asked me who'd been at the stalls. I told him. Every name.
b : Turnabout. | Do they ask often? | Every name?
a : Turnabout, aye. I enjoy it. | Every week. I make them wait. | Every one. Loudly.

scene grown_gossip
when topic=gossip here.region=ridgemere
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : Heard? #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#! The whole pump's saying so. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Twice by noon. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. You'd hear anyway, so I'm telling you.
b : Not so loud. | Twice? | I hadn't.
a : I don't do not so loud. | Twice is true. Three's certain. | Now you have.

scene grown_festival
when topic=festival here.region=ridgemere
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Festival! I'm calling the whole square. They asked me. | The loudest day of the year. My day. | I'll do every cry at the festival, and then I'll sleep for two days.
b : They asked you? | Your day? | Two days?
a : Asked me! Me! I'd have done it anyway. | Mine. Everyone else just borrows it. | Two. And next year, all over.

scene grown_newcomer
when topic=newcomer here.region=ridgemere
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #topic.subject.capitalize# is new, they say. By Restday I'll know the lot. | There's a new one. #topic.subject.capitalize#. I'll go and have a look. | #topic.subject.capitalize# means to stop here, I'm told. Good. Another voice for the square.
b : Leave #topic.them# be. | Have a look? | Another voice?
a : After I've had a look. | Just a look. And a word. Several words. | Another voice. The more the louder.

rule @grown_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere here.time=day
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Fish! Fresh off the boat! | Hot bread! Hot bread by the steps!

dlg @6 resident.hub : #greet#! You're new to the square, I'd know you otherwise. | #greet#. Ask me anything about the square. I know it.
dlg @4 resident.job : I call the square. Sales, stalls, anything. My voice does the rest. | Whatever the square says, I shout back louder. It's a living.
dlg @2 resident.bye : #farewell#! Listen for me. | Bye! You'll hear me from the steps.

young
line @1 greet : #greet#! I'm being the fish stall. | Hello! Listen to me.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Hello. You're new. I know everyone. | #greet#. You're new. I'm the fish stall today.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#! | Hello again!
line @1 farewell : Bye! Square's waiting. | Bye, bye, bye!
line @1 farewell.return : Bye! | Bye! Shout if you want me.
line @1 react.news : Tell me! Tell me! | What? What happened?
line @1 react.news.new : I didn't know that! | Nobody told me!
line @1 answer.how : Loud! | Hungry. And loud.
line @1 decline : No! I don't want to and I won't. | I'm not doing that. It's not fair.
line @1 accept_decline : Fine. | All right, then.
line @1 thank : Thank you! | Thanks!
line @1 ack : Mm! | Mm-hm.
scene ad_fish_stall
when topic=pastimes|day here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fish! Fresh off the boat! That's me being the fish stall. | I can do the onion stall too. Onions! Onions! | I shouted like the fish stall and the fish wolf looked round.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : That's very good, little one. | Not so loud, please. | Did they?
b : That's good! | Do it again! | Ha!
a@grown : I know. I'm the best at it. | That's not loud. This is loud. | Always. Never fails.
a : I'm the best. | Fish! Fresh off the boat! | Ha!

scene ad_birds
when topic=animals here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A bird on the gutter's shouting at me. I'm shouting back. | The sparrows took my crust. I let them. They looked hungry. | I watched the birds fight. The little one won.
b : Who's louder? | That was kind. | The little one!
a : Me. | They were. So was I. | The little one always wins. I'm the little one.

scene ad_stew
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I had stew. Mutton stew. It was the best. | I want stew. Is there stew? | There was stew at the chapel. I had it all.
b : Lucky you. | Not today. | All of it?
a : Lucky me. | Tomorrow, then. | All. And the bread.

rule @ad_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Fish! Fish! | Onions! Onions!

dlg @5 resident.hub : Hello! I can do the fish stall. Listen. | Hello! I'm loud. Did you know?
dlg @3 resident.job : I'm a pup. I do the stall cries. | I play on the square. I shout.

adolescent
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You're new. I'd know you otherwise; I know everybody on this square. | #greet#! New face. Lost, or just looking? Looking, I'd say.
line @2 greet : #greet#! | #greet#. Listen to the square today, it's lovely.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. The stalls aren't even up. I came to watch them go up. | Morning. First one on the square, me.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. The square's packing up. Saddest bit of the day. | Evening. It's all gone quiet. I hate quiet.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. I've loads to tell you. | Sit down, sit down, wait till you hear.
line @1 again.open : You again! Good. I've more since. | Back already. Good, there's more.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#! | #greet#. You heard me from the pump, I bet.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : Oh, good, it's you. Listen. | You came back. Good. I've the best one yet.
line @1 farewell : Right. The fish stall's starting. #farewell#. | #farewell#. I'll see you on the square, I always do.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Night. The square's shut anyway. | #farewell#. Mind the wet cobbles by the pump.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#! | Bye, then. Holler, and I'll come.
line @1 react.news : Go on. Go on, then! | Tell me everything. Slowly. No, quickly.
line @1 react.news.new : I hadn't heard! I hear everything. How did I miss that? | Nobody on the square's said that. Not yet.
line @1 react.news.known : Oh, that. The whole square had that by noon. | I knew. The fish stall had it first.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That's not what they're saying at the pump, and the pump's always right. | Who said? Because if it's who I think, I'd not believe it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh no. That's horrid. That's really horrid. | That's awful. The whole square will be quiet tomorrow.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Oh, lovely! I'll tell everyone. | That's the best news all week.
line @1 answer.how : Hungry. Loud. Fine. | Good! Better when the square's full.
line @1 ask.how : You all right? You've a rainy-day look. | Have you eaten? Properly?
line @1 sympathise : Oh, that's rotten. Sit here. Talk. | That's horrid. I'd shout at somebody, if I were you.
line @1 reassure : It'll pass. Everything does, except the rain. | You'll be fine. I'd know if you weren't.
line @1 decline : No, I can't, there's lessons and I'm late as it is and I'll catch it. | Not that. I'm proud, not daft, and no amount of asking will shift me.
line @1 accept_decline : Fine. Your loss. | All right. I'll ask somebody else, then.
line @1 thank : Thanks! Really. I'll not forget. | Oh, that's kind. You didn't have to.
line @1 deflect_thanks : That? Anybody'd do it. | Pfft. Don't. Honestly.
line @1 preclose : The fish stall's starting up. I have to go. | I'd stay, but the square's calling.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. Bye! | Fine, fine. Off you go.
line @1 ack : #bc_right# | Mm! #bc_go_on#
line @1 take_offence : I'm not begging. I'm standing. There's a difference. | Mind how you speak to me. The square's as much mine as yours.
scene stall_cries
when topic=pastimes|day here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Listen. That's the fish stall. Now the onion stall. Now the old cheese wolf. | I can do every stall on the square. Every single one. Want to hear? | The eel stall's the hardest. It lifts on the last word. Like this.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : You've got the onion one exactly. | Go on, then. Just one. | You'll get yourself in trouble doing that.
b : That's very good. | Go on, then. | It does go up!
a@grown : Exactly. It's my best. I've practised it on the stairs. | Fish! Fresh off the boat! There, that's the fish. | Trouble's only when they hear. They always hear.
a : I know. I'm the best at it. Ask anybody on the square. | Fish! Fresh off the boat! That's the fish one. | It does. Nobody else notices. I notice.

scene marketday_crush
when topic=day|pastimes here.day=market here.region=ridgemere
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Marketday! #crowd.capitalize#. Drop me in the middle and leave me there. | Everybody's shouting, everybody's pushing, everybody's here. Nothing beats it. | I can hear six stalls at once from the pump. Six! I counted.
b : It's too busy for me. | Mind your pockets. | Six?
a : Too busy's the point! Quiet days are for sleeping. | Nothing in my pockets to mind. Saves worrying. | Six. Seven if the eel stall's going.

scene roof_birds
when topic=animals here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #birds.capitalize# have a market of their own on the gutters. They shout worse than the stalls. | There's one sparrow who steals from the bread stall every day. I've named it. | I give my crusts to the gutter birds. Well. I give the ones I can't eat.
b : They do fight. | What's it called? | Kind of you.
a : Over everything! Crusts, gutters, nothing at all. Like stallholders. | I call it thief. It knows. It doesn't care. | It's not kind. They're loud and they're mine.

scene mutton_stew
when topic=food
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #stew.capitalize#. If I had one every day, I'd be the happiest wolf on the hill. | The chapel did mutton stew on Restday. I had two bowls. Nobody stopped me. | The pie stall's stew is all gravy. Proper stew, you can stand a spoon up.
b : Two bowls? | That's the best. | Gravy's not so bad.
a : Two! And bread. I could have done three. | It is. Nothing beats it. Not even eel. | Gravy's fine. Gravy's not stew.

scene autumn_wind
when topic=weather|season here.season=autumn here.weather=clear|overcast
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #autumnwind.capitalize#. Look at the leaves going round the pump! | I love this. Everything blowing about and everyone holding their hats. | Wind like this, the stall awnings go like sails. Somebody always loses one.
b : It's cold. | Hold on to yours. | Did anyone lose one?
a : It's lively! Cold's fine if it's lively. | I've no hat. That's my secret. | The cloth stall! Last week! I saw it go right over the Market Hall.

scene salt_wind
when topic=weather here.weather=overcast|storm here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Ugh. #saltwind.capitalize#. It's the only wind I hate. | Sea wind again. It makes my fur stiff and it makes the square empty. | It's blowing off the water. Everyone goes home and the square's dead.
b : It does bite. | Brush it out. | It'll turn.
a : It bites and it stinks of the wharf. Horrid. | Brush it with what? I've got paws. | It better. A dead square's the worst thing there is.

scene wet_floor
when topic=weather|home here.weather=rain|storm
does tell.complaint / sympathise / assess
a : #wetfloor.capitalize# again. The rain comes under our door like it lives there. | I can't sit anywhere. Everything's wet. The floor's wet. My tail's wet. | When it rains the floor goes dark and cold and I sit on the bed with my paws up.
b : That's miserable. | Find a dry spot. | Poor you.
a : It's miserable! I'd shout at the rain if it listened. | There isn't one. I've looked. Twice. | I'm not poor me. I'm cross me. There's a difference.

scene moved_on
when topic=smalltalk|crime here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint.agree / assess
a : #watch.capitalize# moved me off the Market Hall steps. I was only sitting! | I got told to move along. Move along where? Everywhere's somewhere. | A watchman said I was in the way. I'm small. I'm not in anybody's way.
b : That's not fair. | They do that. | You're a bit in the way.
a : It's not fair, and I said as much. Loudly. | Daily they shift me. Daily I come back. | I'm not. I'm exactly where I should be.

scene dole_line
when topic=times|smalltalk self.on_dole=yes here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'm in the dole line Restday. I'll do the stall cries to pass the time. Folk laugh. | The dole line's quiet. I hate quiet lines. So I talk. | You see everybody in the dole line. Everybody. You'd be surprised.
b : That's one way to wait. | Do they mind? | Who?
a : It's the only way. Waiting quiet is the worst thing. | Some do. Some talk back. Those are the good ones. | Not telling. It's not my business. I'll tell you if you're in it.

scene not_a_beggar
when topic=smalltalk|times here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A lady on the square held out a copper to me. I'm not begging! I was listening. | Somebody wanted to know if I'd lost my way. I live here. I'm not lost. | A traveller called me poor thing. I'm not a poor thing. I'm loud.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : I'm sure she meant it kindly. | Sorry. I thought you might be. | It was meant kindly.
b : That's rude. | They didn't know. | Some people.
a@grown : Kindly's fine. I'll take it kindly and give it back. | Well. Now you know. I'm never lost. | Fine. But I'm still not a poor thing.
a : Rude! I'd have said so but my mouth was full. | They know now. I told them. Loudly. | Some people. I said so to her face.

scene lessons
when topic=work|day self.job=child
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Lessons all morning. Quiet all morning. I nearly burst. | The teacher said I'm too loud. I said I'm exactly loud enough. | I'd rather be on the square, but I go. I'm not daft.
b : It's good for you. | You are a bit loud. | Good.
a : Maybe. It's still quiet. | A bit loud is the right amount. | Not daft. Just loud.

scene gossip_loud
when topic=gossip here.region=ridgemere
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : Have you heard? #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#! Everybody at the pump's saying so. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. The bread stall had it. Then the fish stall. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. I'm only telling you because you'd hear anyway.
b : Keep your voice down. | Twice? | I hadn't.
a : I don't keep it down. It doesn't go down. | Twice is true. Three times is certain. | Now you have. You're welcome.

scene gossip_sad
when topic=gossip topic.claim_kind=death
does tell.news / sympathise / assess
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. The square was quiet all morning. I hated it. | It came round the pump this morning. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. I didn't do any cries today. It didn't seem right.
b : That's sad. | Poor soul. | Good of you.
a : It is sad. I don't like sad. It's too quiet. | Poor soul. I'll do a cry tomorrow for #topic.them#. A quiet one. | Not good. Just proper.

scene festival_noise
when topic=festival here.region=ridgemere
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Festival! The square's louder than it's ever been. And I'll be stood right in it. | I'm going to do every cry on the square at the festival. Every one. People will pay. | There's music, and shouting, and food, and everybody's out. I tick the days off on the wall.
b : Don't get lost. | Pay? | Every year.
a : Lost? On my own square? Never. | They might! I'll take a hat round. If I find a hat. | Every year. I count the days.

scene newcomer_seen
when topic=newcomer here.region=ridgemere
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #topic.subject.capitalize# is new, they say! I'll go and have a look on the square. | New in the city: #topic.subject#. Give me till Restday and I'll know everything. | #topic.subject.capitalize# means to stop here, I'm told. Good. The square needs more voices.
b : Leave #topic.them# be. | By Restday? | More voices?
a : I'll leave #topic.them# be after I've had a look. | Restday. Maybe Marketday. I'm quick. | More voices, more noise, better square.

scene crier_dream
when topic=dreams|work here.region=ridgemere
does confide / react.self / assess
a : I'm going to be #crier#. Calling the sales. Everyone will have to listen. | One day the whole square will stop when I shout. Like it does for the bell. | The crier's voice is nothing. Mine's better. Don't tell the crier.
b : You'd be good at it. | Like the bell? | I won't.
a : I'd be the best. I already am, nearly. | Louder than the bell. The bell can't do the fish stall. | You'd better not. I'm keeping it for when I'm grown.

story first_cry [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=10]
  : The first cry I learned was the onion stall. Onions, sweet onions, three a copper.
  : I said it so loud the onion wolf turned round to see who was selling.
  : The whole square laughed. Even the onion wolf.
  ask : Were you ever loud enough to turn a whole street round?
  b : Never. I'd have died of shame. Did you?
  : No. I did it again. Louder.

story lost_hat [topic=weather|season self.age>=10 here.region=ridgemere]
  : One autumn the wind took the cloth stall's awning clean off.
  : It went up over the square like a gull, and everybody stopped shouting to watch it.
  : Only me kept shouting. I shouted where it was headed.
  b : Did anybody catch it?
  : I did. On the Market Hall steps. They gave me a pie.

story pie_reward [topic=food|memories self.age>=10 here.region=ridgemere]
  : Once I stood all day by the pie stall doing its cry better than the pie wolf.
  : By dusk the pie wolf gave up and let me shout, and sold out before dark.
  : I got the last pie, burnt at one end. Best thing I ever ate.
  b : You earned it. Did they ask you back?
  : Every Marketday since. Burnt end and all.

rule @bark_cry
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere here.time=day
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Fish! Fresh off the boat! | Onions, sweet onions, three a copper!

rule @bark_saltwind
when concept=bark here.weather=overcast|storm
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Ugh. That wind. | Everyone's going home. Don't go home!

rule @bark_birds
when concept=bark here.weather=clear|overcast
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Oi! Put that crust back, you thief! | Look at them fight up there.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#! I know everybody on this square, so you're new. | #greet#. If you want to know anything, ask me. I know it.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#! You're back. I knew you'd be back. | Oh, it's #topic.player#. Good. Listen.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Night. The square's dead. Talk to me, then. | It's late. I'm not tired. What is it?
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Come closer and I'll yell the square down. I can, too. | Stop there. Say what you're after.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#, when I have to be. Otherwise I'm on the square. | Lessons. And the square. And the stall cries. All of them.
dlg @2 resident.job : I listen to the square. Somebody should. | I'm going to be the crier. I'm practising.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : They're saying at the pump, from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. | Heard it on the square, from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. Everyone knows.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : It's all #world.event_words# from the pump to the steps. | It's #world.event_words#! Everybody's shouting about it.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Not on the square, anyway. | Nothing! Can you believe it? Nothing at all.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Have you heard? #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. Everybody's saying. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Twice I've had it today.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : Nothing! It's been so quiet. | #gossip_none# Which I hate.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#! I'll see you on the square. | Bye! Listen for me. You'll hear me.
graft resident.hub
choice Can you really do every stall's cry? -> cries
node cries
say Every one on the square. Fish, onions, the cheese stall, the eel stall that lifts on the last word. Listen. Fish! Fresh off the boat!
mood keen
free
choice Do the onion one. -> cries_onion
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node cries_onion
say Onions, sweet onions, three a copper! There. The onion wolf turns round every time. Never fails.
choice That's very good. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
